  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>If the resistance of the wire is <em>R</em>, then each arm of the square has a resistance of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>R</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>. Accordingly. The resistance of segments DE and EC are&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>DE</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>EC</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>R</mi><mn>8</mn></mfrac></math>.</p><p>We can draw the resultant circuit as follows:</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/57bc8af5-690a-4e71-96db-e5d87a403501-image.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 287px;\" /></p><p>Hence,</p><p><math><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>7</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><math><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>56</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>7</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>7</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>64</mn></mrow></mfrac></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
